Date: Thu, 3 Sep 2026 05:16:56 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 016/105] spec: remove per-draft-step glue in the topk=1 chain
 with a hot-vocab map

- draft_topk1_postprocess: optional hot_token_id map applied inside the
  finalize kernel, so the direct draft_tokens_topk1 chain path (no per-step
  select_top_k_tokens, no separate gather) now also covers
  --speculative-token-map serving.
- QSA MTP shared sparse-index lookup: one Triton kernel replaces the ~10
  torch ops (gather/cast/arange/where/slice-assign) per draft step.
- GPU tests: test/srt/speculative/test_draft_fuse.py (8 passed), existing
  topk1 fastpath tests (9 passed).

Implemented by Codex (gpt-5.6-sol) from DRAFT_FUSE_SPEC.md; reviewed and
GPU-validated by the supervisor.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
